{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot","id":1429791,"title":"Why doesn\u2019t Exalted have a metaplot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-24T16:38:40-08:00","id":1429791,"title":"Why doesn\u2019t Exalted have a metaplot?","content":"Should it have one?<br /> <br /> I think it would be cool. I like games that are more like interactive novels or TV shows. But I also know that other people\u2019s views may differ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T17:06:53-08:00","id":1429794,"title":"","content":"Metaplot is always a bad idea, IMO. Especially in such a high-powered game as Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T17:31:11-08:00","id":1429797,"title":"","content":"Why is it a bad idea? It gives you cool NPCs to interact with and a backdrop of other events that are happening while your characters are doing their thing. Plus like I said you can follow the plot like a novel. Or am I misunderstanding the word metaplot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T17:33:54-08:00","id":1429798,"title":"","content":"I think it makes the world seem more alive, like stuff is happening, not just sitting there static waiting for your PCs to do stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T17:58:05-08:00","id":1429804,"title":"","content":"I don't like it because it locks you into things that I as an ST might not want. Like if the metaplot is like &quot;The Locust Crusade is happening now!&quot; or &quot;The Reclamation is tipping off!&quot; then all of a sudden I can't do the things I was wanting to do.<br /> <br /> I mean, I could, I could just tell my players &quot;we're not doing metaplot stuff&quot; but for one, they'll be following it and expecting it, and for another that metaplot material is taking the place of more setting stuff that I could actually be using.<br /> <br /> The closest thing we have right now to a metaplot is Jiara, where the main Solar circle exalted there, then house Mnemon came and drove them into the hinterlands. That's just one satrapy among hundreds, and it doesn't really affect the rest of the world much, except that Mnemon is probably IN Jiara, so already if I want her to show up in the Imperial City or something my players might be like &quot;Yo, isn't she fighting Solars in one of her satrapies? What's she doing here? Did she win?&quot; and I don't want to have to do that for another hundred nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T18:01:59-08:00","id":1429806,"title":"","content":"So, first of all, I'd like to define &quot;metaplot&quot; so that we're on the same page. I define it as being a thing where events in the game's fictional history &quot;progress&quot; over the course of the game line: things happen that change the status quo, and later supplements reference the new state of affairs. That established, I think there's a couple problems with doing things that way with Exalted.<br /> <br /> First, the problem that's common to more or less all instances of metaplot: it tends to be offputting to fans who aren't able or willing to buy every book. Imagine that the corebook presented a city (Gem, say) as being a thriving community. Then a sourcebook comes out that has Gem blow up. Sourcebooks published after that then refer to Gem as being a destroyed ruin. If someone hasn't had a chance to purchase the book where Gem was declared destroyed, they can very easily become confused when a reference to it mentions it being a crater. &quot;Wait, I thought it was a major city in the South? What <i>happened?&quot;</i> Or, if the latter books try to explain the metaplot, they end up having to waste a bunch of wordcount doing that. If every book released after Gem gets destroyed has a paragraph saying &quot;Oh BTW Gem was blown up, here's the short version&quot;, people who <i>do</i> have the book where it happened are likely to get sick of <i>that</i>, and it's probably <i>still</i> not very clear to people who didn't purchase it.<br /> <br /> Besides being annoying if you haven't read the book where something important happened, it's also likely to annoy people who were planning to use a location or NPC in a different way. If I read the description of Gem in the corebook and thought &quot;hey, that sounds cool, I'm going to set my campaign there!&quot;, I'm not likely to be happy when the sourcebook on Gem blows it up, and then all the later books only talk about it in terms of it being destroyed. That basically makes all those books useless to me for my Gem campaign. It's always easier to let GMs change details from what's been presented in the setting, rather than forcing the changes on them.<br /> <br /> The other problem with metaplot is more Exalted-centric. Metaplot, in general, is good for giving a setting a sense of moving forward, of getting the PCs to react to a changing setting. But Exalted is, by design, a setting where the players are expected to be much more pro-active. They're <i>supposed </i>to be going out and changing the world, shaking the pillars of Heaven, etc. Maybe not universally on the scale of the whole world, but at the very least, on their local level. That means that there's much less likely to be a comfortable status quo that the players have gotten used to, and much more likely that they've already made significant changes of their own accord. The changes to the setting that a metaplot implies would almost certainly contradict that, for virtually every campaign. For example, consider probably the most likely metaplot event: the Realm Civil War kicks off. The Civil War is very, very likely to be a central thing for virtually every Dynastic Dragon-Blood chronicle. And it's a thing that is incredibly dependent on initial conditions. Does it kick off because a Mnemon PC insults a scion of Nellens? Does the House Tepet character make a play for restoring her family's prestige? And so on. Having the setting book come in and say &quot;the Civil War starts when House Ragara teams up with Sesus and Peleps, with these specific NPCs behind it&quot; just isn't going to work with most games, and thus the information the books provide will just be less and less useful for practically everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just as a final note, I'd point out that the closest thing that Exalted has had to a metaplot was the release of Return of the Scarlet Empress, late in the 2e line. And that is <i>not</i> a book I'd consider as being remembered particularly well in the fandom. I mean, it had problems outside the fact that it was kinda-sorta metaplot. But the &quot;we don't want metaplot&quot; element was definitely, I feel, a significant part of its poor reception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T18:04:25-08:00","id":1429808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429804#post1429804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest thing we have right now to a metaplot is Jiara, where the main Solar circle exalted there, then house Mnemon came and drove them into the hinterlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that even the idea that it's the signature Solar Circle isn't actually canon - we know there's some Solars there, but the only thing that suggests that it's the signatures is the chapter fiction, and that's not considered canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T18:41:01-08:00","id":1429813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429808#post1429808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that even the idea that it's the signature Solar Circle isn't actually canon - we know there's some Solars there, but the only thing that suggests that it's the signatures is the chapter fiction, and that's not considered canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is good, I\u2019m happy to hear it, I think it goes to show how pervasive even an implied and explicitly non-canon metaphor can be. <br /> <br /> Like people used to point out all the time that RotSE isn\u2019t canon and you can just ignore it, but that didn\u2019t stop basically every game post RotSE feeling like it had to deal with it in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T19:36:55-08:00","id":1429820,"title":"","content":"I will add that an issue with metaplot is also when things move on and old plot points are resolved. I remember a bit of annoyance and frustration when the big bad was supposed to get in good with the local hierarchy in one game courtesy of how the big bad had shown up and annihilated the previous big bad when the players had handled that problem themselves. So in order to incorporate that Big Bad and the plot as the setup is being done means a new existential threat of actually greater threat needs to be imagined as something the big bad took out in order to explain why this being has more clout than the PCs do, and that's not incorporating any mcguffins that are supposed to have been transferred between big bads that the PCs might have acquired, destroyed, etc; or if the PCs had resolved the plot in any way that nullified the previous threat without its destruction that the metaplot can't account for due to it no longer existing.<br /> <br /> Now granted these are hardly impossible to deal with, but it is annoying and causes chunks of the book to just be utterly useless to you because they're all dealing with the armies and horrors the blind man let loose trying to bring the Primogenitor into the world and how that's screwed up the setting, which is just really not helpful for your group as Insatiables are just flat-out no's for your group that they don't want to deal with for reasons. Then you end up with arguments and debates on how things have to be because of blah blah blah.*<br /> <br /> *Oh my god so many arguments on how stupid everything was because RotSE meant &quot;well cannonically the Infernals win and not acknowledging that is just stupid.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T19:38:43-08:00","id":1429821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429806#post1429806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a final note, I'd point out that the closest thing that Exalted has had to a metaplot was the release of Return of the Scarlet Empress, late in the 2e line. And that is <i>not</i> a book I'd consider as being remembered particularly well in the fandom. I mean, it had problems outside the fact that it was kinda-sorta metaplot. But the &amp;quot;we don't want metaplot&amp;quot; element was definitely, I feel, a significant part of its poor reception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you said, but just a tiny bit of additional context for this one: RotSE was, as made pretty clearly from it's afterword, at time of writing expected to be the last Exalted book. Which is doubly noteworthy as the &quot;only&quot; metaplot book; it's like the final resolution of any &quot;will they/won't they&quot; plot arc for long time series fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T21:16:22-08:00","id":1429825,"title":"","content":"Metaplot is Lucy Van Pelt, constantly yanking the football away. Charlie Brown might never learn, but I do. I don't pay one red cent for games contaminated with metaplot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T21:44:49-08:00","id":1429827,"title":"","content":"1e also had the <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians</b> stories. Which were similarly not very canon. ANd also kind of train wrecks.<br /> <br /> In general, a lot of the maint hings were covered. A big thing ton ote is that RPG settings are not ficiton settings. They shoudl be places that are friendly for players to operate in. And while there is some funin reading about what happens next in a metaplot, they are rarely in service of actually presenting interesting stuff. This is especially ahrd to do well in a game like Exalted, where relaly more aobut hte setting at Time Zero is actually giong to be more useufl since the world is well, big, and finidng out what is there is more important than what happens next.<br /> <br /> Metaplots also have a bit of a habit of &quot;eating&quot; setting formaiton from above. The Gem thing is good exmaple, but note also this means that to talk more about what happened to Gem is time nto talking about a different place or how Gem is useful somewhere lse. And it also often to be notable has been something &quot;wroth the time of Exalted&quot;, whcih also could lead to overvaluing the importance of things.<br /> <br /> A good example of this is the takes on the Locust Crusade presented between <b>Time of Tumult</b>'s &quot;Crusaders of the Machine God&quot; chapter and <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians</b> &quot;The Locust War&quot;. They broaldy, cover the ame events, but I think the latter is more &quot;metaplotty.&quot; It ties in with more of the setting, tries to bring in key named NPCs into the events like Deathlords, and Great House contenders, and even ends with a big fight of the Kukla and a thousand fourged dragon. The original chapter was by contrast a detail of new locations, new entities, and the end story resulted in the establishmen tof a potential new empire on the map. The later chatper by contrast more or less became an Avengers style existential world thing that invovled everyhone ever named. ANd while htose coudl be fun, the latter is just striaght up less useful to most games, but I think mor eindicative of the storts of storie syou get in metaplots.<br /> <br /> ANother one is kind of in video games to me. I love the Mass Effect setting as presented in the first game. But due to the story of the game, while good for that trilogy, it kind of just is...done at end there. ANd I think that the stting as ar esult is less useable for future media like more sequels or RPGs, becuase the setting has this overarching fixed metaplot that by it send blows the entire setting up and leaves you with a start of game satus quo and whatever the post-Reaper settin gis. And I think Exalted's attempts of long story campaigns tned to look like that, and are just not something sustainable for a setting as big as it is and wiht the kinds of stories itw ants to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T21:45:12-08:00","id":1429828,"title":"","content":"WoD tried it, Exalted flirted with it. Both cases sucked, in no small part because, inherently, metaplots determine the course of the story. Overall an open playground just runs better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T22:42:10-08:00","id":1429830,"title":"","content":"I personally think having a metaplot in a TTRPG is a fool's errand. Especially, as noted, in a game like Exalted. Because you're playing as Exalts, which will likely make waves.<br /> <br /> Let's take, for instance, the War for the Throne in the Realm. In 2e, it was assumed that the Realm was just about to hit full Civil War, with a lot of families, groups, and players pushing for advantage. This is <i>great</i>, I should mention, because it gives a lot of opportunity to play with or against the situation.<br /> <br /> However, imagine... At one point a supplement goes &quot;In the aftermath of the Realm Civil War, the one who took the throne was in fact Ledaal Kes. This is how the game will assume history goes going forward&quot;<br /> <br /> While not a bad result, giving an ironclad statement like that can give a feeling of invalidation to cases where Ledaal Kes did not take the Scarlet Throne, such as if a Dynast game had the PCs back Mnemon, or some people put Ejava on the throne, or something more outlandish. Or for something majorly intense, like the PCs striking while the Realm was weak to destroy the entire empire.<br /> <br /> No, I think Exalted is best off by establishing: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Who the major players and what the major events/situations are</li> <li>MAYBE allude to intentions and what may happen Soon or Eventually, but NOT write future books with the assumption that they go that way.</li> </ol><br /> An example of this done decently is in the manuscript for the Dragonblood Companion (distributed to those who backed the DB book) which talks about a POTENTIAL (it says this very often) future for the Realm as a story SUGGESTION. It mentions things like &quot;If the PCs don't intervene here, then House Peleps will-&quot; and the like. Plus it also gives multiple outcomes as suggestions for the GM to roll with, depending on player action.<br /> <br /> Going &quot;This is how things stand NOW&quot; suits Exalted better, because many players will read that and will plot on how to interact with that. Some may go &quot;Time to ruin stuff&quot;, some may go &quot;Time to help these people&quot;, and for things like adventure modules suggested paths and likely outcomes are great, but it shouldn't be assumed that Outcome 4B from the <b>Mnemon's Birthday Bonanza</b> Adventure Module is the canon outcome that will influence the upcoming setting book: <b>1001 Creation-Shaking Disasters</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T23:19:17-08:00","id":1429831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429830#post1429830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think having a metaplot in a TTRPG is a fool's errand. Especially, as noted, in a game like Exalted. Because you're playing as Exalts, which will likely make waves.<br /> <br /> Let's take, for instance, the War for the Throne in the Realm. In 2e, it was assumed that the Realm was just about to hit full Civil War, with a lot of families, groups, and players pushing for advantage. This is <i>great</i>, I should mention, because it gives a lot of opportunity to play with or against the situation.<br /> <br /> However, imagine... At one point a supplement goes &amp;quot;In the aftermath of the Realm Civil War, the one who took the throne was in fact Ledaal Kes. This is how the game will assume history goes going forward&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> While not a bad result, giving an ironclad statement like that can give a feeling of invalidation to cases where Ledaal Kes did not take the Scarlet Throne, such as if a Dynast game had the PCs back Mnemon, or some people put Ejava on the throne, or something more outlandish. Or for something majorly intense, like the PCs striking while the Realm was weak to destroy the entire empire.<br /> <br /> No, I think Exalted is best off by establishing: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Who the major players and what the major events/situations are</li> <li>MAYBE allude to intentions and what may happen Soon or Eventually, but NOT write future books with the assumption that they go that way.</li> </ol><br /> An example of this done decently is in the manuscript for the Dragonblood Companion (distributed to those who backed the DB book) which talks about a POTENTIAL (it says this very often) future for the Realm as a story SUGGESTION. It mentions things like &amp;quot;If the PCs don't intervene here, then House Peleps will-&amp;quot; and the like. Plus it also gives multiple outcomes as suggestions for the GM to roll with, depending on player action.<br /> <br /> Going &amp;quot;This is how things stand NOW&amp;quot; suits Exalted better, because many players will read that and will plot on how to interact with that. Some may go &amp;quot;Time to ruin stuff&amp;quot;, some may go &amp;quot;Time to help these people&amp;quot;, and for things like adventure modules suggested paths and likely outcomes are great, but it shouldn't be assumed that Outcome 4B from the <b>Mnemon's Birthday Bonanza</b> Adventure Module is the canon outcome that will influence the upcoming setting book: <b>1001 Creation-Shaking Disasters</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I see your point. I guess metaplots aren\u2019t that great. I\u2019ve never run an RPG besides D&amp;D and I\u2019ve never even played Exalted (I just think the setting\u2019s pretty cool), so I never really thought of a lot of the points you guys raised.<br /> <br /> But that still leaves two other questions: how do you advance the time frame? (like what happens when you want to play the children and grandchildren of your original characters several decades in the future and you have no source material to back it up?) and how do you deal with people who actually like buying every product and reading RPG settings as fiction? (I guess by writing actual novels?)<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T00:34:42-08:00","id":1429833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429831#post1429831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do you advance the time frame? (like what happens when you want to play the children and grandchildren of your original characters several decades in the future and you have no source material to back it up?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you want that? The children and grandchildren of your Exalted characters are probably going to be mortal or only slightly better, and you are capable of outliving them by huge orders of magnitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and how do you deal with people who actually like buying every product and reading RPG settings as fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fangs at the Gate describes an entirely different side of the world than What Fire Has Wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T00:56:20-08:00","id":1429834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429833#post1429833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would you want that? The children and grandchildren of your Exalted characters are probably going to be mortal or only slightly better, and you are capable of outliving them by huge orders of magnitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you wanted to play a mortal game about characters with the shared circumstances of trying to forge their place in the world under the shadow of their legendary grandparents, I could see it. More likely, you'd run a game with powerful characters unrelated to your former characters, but affected by the world altering actions they took. You'd still have to keep track of the sweeping changes and compare them with the locations you're going to run your game in and then consider how the places might be changed because of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T01:33:58-08:00","id":1429837,"title":"","content":"I personally love metaplot in ttrpgs. I feel like it adds a bit more soul to the setting, and can bring about some fun to toy around with. Obviously some people really dislike metaphor, but I find it super easy to just disregard what I don't like and add in new things they create. (It might be a result of being an avid reader/writer of both original and fan content, so I'm quite adept at dissecting what I dislike from things I like.)<br /> I feel like too many settings in ttrpgs these days are abandoning metaphor in newer editions and it really just gives me the feeling of lacking soul. <br /> Also, I absolutely love when games have clues and things that are later revealed in metaplot and you're like &quot;I was right?!&quot; Or when a character you hated has had something happen off page and comes back slightly different and you actually get really invested in them. *Chef kiss*<br /> As always in ttrpg, some people will adore it and some will despise it. I think it would add some flair to later additions, so like if something really cool gets thought up, you can create an event to introduce it, so it doesn't just feel like a retroactive insert. <br /> Yes, it might invalidate some people's games, but there is nothing stating you have to use it, but it can give more cohesion to a setting that uses staggered releases, since that can do the same thing as metaplot does, as a splatbook or setting book is going to contain more info that the core has on new things, so by the time it comes out, you have either just treated it like it wasn't there ever, like it was always there it just never ever came up, or the book will invalidate what you have already come up with.<br /> There are arguments to be had for both sides. I personally just think ttrpgs with metaplots are better than metaplot-lite, or worse metaplot-less, settings and franchises. <br /> To each there own, as they say. If they had one, I'd be happy, if they didn't I'd deal with it and just acknowledge that it's a static starting line in setting and work from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T02:01:58-08:00","id":1429838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429831#post1429831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. I see your point. I guess metaplots aren\u2019t that great. I\u2019ve never run an RPG besides D&amp;D and I\u2019ve never even played Exalted (I just think the setting\u2019s pretty cool), so I never really thought of a lot of the points you guys raised.<br /> <br /> But that still leaves two other questions: how do you advance the time frame? (like what happens when you want to play the children and grandchildren of your original characters several decades in the future and you have no source material to back it up?) and how do you deal with people who actually like buying every product and reading RPG settings as fiction? (I guess by writing actual novels?)<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm gonna talk about that last one here, and say that there are a few ways that the books do that. Not just by showing new sides of the setting, but by specifically showing new angles on conflicts established elsewhere. <i>Lunars</i> gives us a new perspective on the conflict in the Caul then Realm or Dragonblooded or the Core did. We'll see if this continues, but I'd describe it as the setting expanding horizontally in time--going deeper into a moment instead of to another moment.<br /> Exalted did try something in <i>Heirs</i>(out to KS atm) by giving insight into the Civil War's potentail shapes. And that path might work in the future, I found it decent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T02:42:57-08:00","id":1429840,"title":"","content":"The only metaplot point I\u2019ve ever actively liked was the one in Shadowrun: Kill Code that ends with \u201cand that\u2019s why grids don\u2019t matter any more.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T04:03:40-08:00","id":1429842,"title":"","content":"While I really don't want metaplot for Exalted, there are good metaplots out there.<br /> <br /> The most important part of a metaplot? It needs to be baked into the structure of the game-line from the get go in a fashion that supports the metaplot approach you're taking. Adding metaplot to a game that wasn't built for it something that has never seen real success.<br /> <br /> The most successful metaplot structure is actually very similar to Exalted: the core book(s) are always set at year 0. Any general setting book, or character expansion book, is also set at year 0. The metaplot only exists in adventure modules.<br /> <br /> The reason this approach can work, is because people that don't like the metaplot get everything they want, but less modules. While people that do like metaplot have one to follow (or multiples, but I don't think I've seen one with multiple mutually exclusive metaplots going on at once).<br /> <br /> This also meshes well with organized play, as what the outcome of a module is, can be determined by the fans that participate in organized play to see what the most popular outcomes were. This helps make groups feel like part of the process.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T04:31:32-08:00","id":1429843,"title":"","content":"I loved Fangs at the Gate and I\u2019m looking forward to Heirs to the Shogunate. And I agree with you guys that the Lunar book adds a lot of depth to the world.<br /> <br /> And I thought all Exalted inherited their parents\u2019 powers, or at least had a chance of inheriting the Exalted gene, like novas can in Aberrant. If I ever run a game I might change the rules, make that a thing. I like complex plots that run through various generations of the same family (even if some people do think they\u2019re elitist).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I Liked your post. Made a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T04:34:55-08:00","id":1429844,"title":"","content":"Also, I just remembered after I wrote that that the Dragon-Blooded are the ones whose powers run in families. Celestial Exalted don\u2019t do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T04:39:19-08:00","id":1429845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KnightFenrirWulfhart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429837#post1429837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally love metaplot in ttrpgs. I feel like it adds a bit more soul to the setting, and can bring about some fun to toy around with. Obviously some people really dislike metaphor, but I find it super easy to just disregard what I don't like and add in new things they create. (It might be a result of being an avid reader/writer of both original and fan content, so I'm quite adept at dissecting what I dislike from things I like.)<br /> I feel like too many settings in ttrpgs these days are abandoning metaphor in newer editions and it really just gives me the feeling of lacking soul. <br /> Also, I absolutely love when games have clues and things that are later revealed in metaplot and you're like &amp;quot;I was right?!&amp;quot; Or when a character you hated has had something happen off page and comes back slightly different and you actually get really invested in them. *Chef kiss*<br /> As always in ttrpg, some people will adore it and some will despise it. I think it would add some flair to later additions, so like if something really cool gets thought up, you can create an event to introduce it, so it doesn't just feel like a retroactive insert. <br /> Yes, it might invalidate some people's games, but there is nothing stating you have to use it, but it can give more cohesion to a setting that uses staggered releases, since that can do the same thing as metaplot does, as a splatbook or setting book is going to contain more info that the core has on new things, so by the time it comes out, you have either just treated it like it wasn't there ever, like it was always there it just never ever came up, or the book will invalidate what you have already come up with.<br /> There are arguments to be had for both sides. I personally just think ttrpgs with metaplots are better than metaplot-lite, or worse metaplot-less, settings and franchises. <br /> To each there own, as they say. If they had one, I'd be happy, if they didn't I'd deal with it and just acknowledge that it's a static starting line in setting and work from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for giving a different viewpoint \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T04:59:31-08:00","id":1429847,"title":"","content":"Start your game with the Balorian Crusade. Boom. 768 years of metaplot. You are welcome.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> RY768 being the &quot;present day&quot; is a spook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>https://post-left.fandom.com/wiki/Max_Stirner</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 'spook' is a controlling abstraction, thought to be existent, thought to have some corporeal foundation but in fact has no physical or material existence and is merely a ghost-like apparition; a phantasm. a spook. Stirner likened spooks to fixed ideas unquestionable doctrines and values that individuals hold very closely and dearly concepts that have latched on to us and take a hold of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Start your game whenever you want. If you want broad strokes plot for how the game is &quot;supposed&quot; to play out, play in a time period where we have established history.<br /> <br /> The most popular Exalted story is almost certainly Keychain of Creation. KoC does <b>not </b>start with RY768 as present day. It describes events that happen before 768, but the comic actually starts in RY788. Because that gives a better story. Start your story whenever works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-25-2020, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T05:53:43-08:00","id":1429848,"title":"","content":"One thing I loved in Trinity Continuum settings, that may be interesting to Exalted, is a \u201cFuture of the Setting\u201d chapter with suggestions to GMs about what may change after year 0 if the characters don\u2019t do anything about. It gives a sense of metaplot without the continual advance of the plot through books.<br /> <br /> It could give hints of how the Civil War would start, or even end, how long it could take, maybe a few ideas for how a reconstruction after the war would go.<br /> <br /> But the main idea is it\u2019s not \u201ccannon\u201d as the ideas are just suggestions to play long runs or even to start campaigns in the aftermath of the war for example. Well, like it was said many times in Trinity forum, Aberrant is the past of Aeon, but Aeon may not be the future of Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T07:08:45-08:00","id":1429853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429831#post1429831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that still leaves two other questions: how do you advance the time frame?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is simply something the Storyteller has to do on their own. Ideally, the setting material provided will suggest ways things could develop (like, if your writeup for Gem says &quot;the Despot of Gem has ambitions to conquer the nearby Tsavo Cities&quot;, it probably makes sense that Gem at least tried to do that in the next 20 years, and has either succeeded or failed, based on what's most interesting for the story). If there's nothing that specific in the writeup, though, the ST will just have to be more creative, thinking up interesting things to have happen in however long it's been since the default setting time. If you're having trouble doing that, I think a useful tactic is to pick a real-world place that kinda-sorta matches the fictional one, and look up what happened to <i>it</i> over the time period in question. Then just &quot;reskin&quot; the real-world events into Exalted (or whichever fantasy/sci-fi world you're talking about). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and how do you deal with people who actually like buying every product and reading RPG settings as fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, no work will satisfy every possible customer. I expect that the people managing and writing the Exalted line have decided that the fraction of the fanbase that treats the game line as a work of fiction and wants an advancing plotline is small enough, compared with the group that wants the books to be a guide to the setting as it exists, and who want information about stuff set in the &quot;default present&quot;, is small enough that they're going to cater to the latter instead. I think it's a reasonable decision, because at least my own experience with the fanbase suggests that the second group is much, much larger than the first. And even if there was a larger fanbase to be attracted by making the books have more of an ongoing plot, that's not particularly certain. RPGs are a business, ultimately. They have to manage risks, and changing the style of a game line in a way that will almost certainly drive off a good chunk of their current fans, to <i>maybe</i> pick up a new fanbase who <i>might</i> be as large or larger than the current one, is a bad gamble unless they have <i>very</i> solid evidence that the second group is actually out there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T07:18:43-08:00","id":1429856,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> thanks! lol That\u2019s actually a great idea. I love historical stuff.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz I loved that about Aeon and Aberrant. I think a lot of people (including me) will wanna know what\u2019s probably gonna happen in the next few years if their characters don\u2019t do anything to change it. That\u2019s even better than a metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T07:48:01-08:00","id":1429860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429848#post1429848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I loved in Trinity Continuum settings, that may be interesting to Exalted, is a \u201cFuture of the Setting\u201d chapter with suggestions to GMs about what may change after year 0 if the characters don\u2019t do anything about. It gives a sense of metaplot without the continual advance of the plot through books.<br /> <br /> It could give hints of how the Civil War would start, or even end, how long it could take, maybe a few ideas for how a reconstruction after the war would go.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will enjoy <i>Heirs of the Shogunate</i> for having exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T09:20:51-08:00","id":1429868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429831#post1429831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> like what happens when you want to play the children and grandchildren of your original characters several decades in the future and you have no source material to back it up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's no possible way a sourcebook could help with a campaign like that. The entire point of jumping a couple decades into the future is to see the effects of choices the players made. Everything, as much as possible, should ripple out from there-- a broad &quot;this is what happened over the next century&quot; would almost certainly contradict what happened on your personal game, at which point why even bother?<br /> <br /> This is all doubly true for Exalted, which more than any other game I've read supports the players dramatically and irreversibly changing the setting. The best you can do is have a personal metaplot by running multiple campaigns in the same version of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T09:38:45-08:00","id":1429871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429868#post1429868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's no possible way a sourcebook could help with a campaign like that. The entire point of jumping a couple decades into the future is to see the effects of choices the players made. Everything, as much as possible, should ripple out from there-- a broad &amp;quot;this is what happened over the next century&amp;quot; would almost certainly contradict what happened on your personal game, at which point why even bother?<br /> <br /> This is all doubly true for Exalted, which more than any other game I've read supports the players dramatically and irreversibly changing the setting. The best you can do is have a personal metaplot by running multiple campaigns in the same version of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a very good point! Thank you \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T11:00:38-08:00","id":1429876,"title":"","content":"I think a game with a metaplot is certainly possible, but it might have to either involve player characters who can't affect the setting enough to really contradict anything in future books, or basically just be a series of published campaigns. Like the game is only Solars, and each year we release a new book detailing what every single group's Solars are up to next as a roller coaster rather than a sandbox. That way nobody can be like &quot;wait, we saved Gem from exploding, how are we headed there in this book?&quot; Because no previous book would imply that you ever saved Gem.<br /> <br /> Which really doesn't work for me having a steady weekly game for years, and sometimes multiple games a week. I need to be able to make my own stories in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T13:52:18-08:00","id":1429894,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of RPGs that are based on existing franchises that struggle with similar problems to metaplot. Star Wars RPGs, for example, have to contend with the fact that new Star Wars stuff is constantly being made, what is and isn't canon has shifted repeatedly, and so on.<br /> <br /> They tend to very much skew towards characters that aren't going to fundamentally change the setting to help with this. This doesn't mean weak characters though. The RPGs of the big comic book universes tend to use the comic book convention to return to normal (even through massive asspulls and retcons) to justify how the setting never really changes. You don't have to worry about your PC group of Batman characters taking down an alliance of rogues, because they'll just escape Arkham again for whatever module/etc. uses them. Hulk punched Omega Red so hard the villain exploded? [Technobabble] held him together just enough he survived it so his healing powers could kick in, and he can show up later despite people thinking the threat was gone.<br /> <br /> But Exalted is designed towards the exact opposite approach to what the PCs should be capable of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T06:06:39-08:00","id":1429932,"title":"","content":"So Exalted is probably like a really bad game to use a metaplot in.<br /> <br /> Thanks guys. This is really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T06:55:30-08:00","id":1429944,"title":"","content":"Just some thoughts.<br /> <br /> Metaplot works in WoD due to the fact that players are supposed to be chumps (I say that endearingly I love the World of Darkness) who are in over their heads while ancient elders engage in a vast Jyhad. In fact the Jyhad or War of Ages that elder vampires were engaged in was one of the central concepts of VtM. And part of the fun of the gameline was following the metaplot and looking for clues to the vast conspiracy to figure out who's doing what and when. Ultimately though when a methuselah kills off a Prince or an Antedluvian wakes up and eats his clan, there's not much that VtM PCs will be able to do about it. For the most part, VtM is a &quot;sink or swim&quot; setting (and to a degree all of the World of Darkness games are too). When the Technocracy obliterates Ravnos with orbital laser beams, that just happens and while that event might alter the course of a campaign, it's not something the PCs would be capable of participating in.<br /> <br /> In fact WoD metaplot adventures that had PC participation (like the Baba Yaga adventure where the PC's basically sit there and watch a bunch of badass elders do badass things but can't really interfere A) because they're not nearly powerful enough and B) would mess with the metaplot) were generally pretty un-fun. The adventures end up feeling very much on-the-rails where you get to look but not interfere. It makes for cool reading but not nearly as cool gaming.<br /> <br /> With Exalted, the players are big damn heroes who are capable of easily changing or altering fate. Metaplot falls on its face when the the new book covering the metaplot says that the Bull of the North just conquered the Linnowan and took over Halta, but in your campaign the PC's murdered him and burned Halta to the ground. The metaplot in WoD would fall aprt too if your PC's could just deflect the Technocracy's space lasers and slap Ravnos back into sanity. That's the sort of thing you can do in Exalted. Ultimately Exalted is designed to be a sandbox game where you have a rich and detailed setting, but the setting is largely frozen in time so that the PCs can do what they want and focus on what they want.<br /> <br /> For the most part I find that as the capabilities of the PC's increase, it begins to cause more and more issues with metaplot. In D&amp;D I ran into this a few times when they would release big metaplot expansions to change stuff around, but I was running a campaign for Epic PCs who would be able to just no-sell those metaplot developments. So I'd have to try to figure out how to have those metaplots happen but not allow the PC's to do anything about it (which the players generally didn't like) or just ignore the metaplot, which is normally what I would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-26-2020, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T09:17:48-08:00","id":1429955,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> okay. I get the impression that Exalted is a particularly bad candidate for metaplot. I\u2019m a (relative) novice to serious RPG play (as opposed to games in middle school and high school that were more about just hanging out) so I didn\u2019t understand that the power level of the PCs made a difference. Thank you guys. Not being snarky; really appreciate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T11:46:44-08:00","id":1429965,"title":"","content":"In 1e and 2e it did. <br /> <br /> 1e had the return of autocthon. 2e had the reclimation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:01:53-08:00","id":1429967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429965#post1429965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e and 2e it did.<br /> <br /> 1e had the return of autocthon. 2e had the reclimation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. The Autochthonia stuff was always optional. &quot;Crusaders of the Machine God&quot; said as much, and things that referred to it said as much. The only references to it were an optional alternative route in <b>Blood &amp; Salt </b>with an &quot;Assuming you used that&quot; rather than the usual metaplot as assumed new canon, and a single texbox in <b>Castebook: Eclipse</b> which again, ran with the logic that by default, it wasn't what the setting assumed, which is not how metaplots usually worked in WW games.<br /> <br /> The <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians </b>was canon, but anything involving contact with Creation was optional. And no ohter books referred to it, in part to being on eof the last books of 1e and the scnearios being different timelines.<br /> <br /> The Reclamation was as a whole part of general setting. It still was all written as if ti were Day Zero, it just added more as to what was going on at Day Zero. The big thing is mostly it had a lot of the hooks cnaonically answered hwen it got to <b>Return of the Scarlet Empress</b>, which itself never was referred to save a single (also optional) adventure module and some mechanics on Yozis that the Ebon Dragon introduced. It was more a sort of setting addition that metaplot as many folks use the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:06:20-08:00","id":1429968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429967#post1429967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda. The Autochthonia stuff was always optional. &quot;Crusaders of the Machine God&quot; said as much, and things that referred to it said as much. The only references to it were an optional alternative route in <b>Blood &amp; Salt </b>with an &quot;Assuming you used that&quot; rather than the usual metaplot as assumed new canon, and a single texbox in <b>Castebook: Eclipse</b> which again, ran with the logic that by default, it wasn't what the setting assumed, which is not how metaplots usually worked in WW games.<br /> <br /> The <b>Exalted: the Autochthonians </b>was canon, but anything involving contact with Creation was optional. And no ohter books referred to it, in part to being on eof the last books of 1e and the scnearios being different timelines.<br /> <br /> The Reclamation was as a whole part of general setting. It still was all written as if ti were Day Zero, it just added more as to what was going on at Day Zero. The big thing is mostly it had a lot of the hooks cnaonically answered hwen it got to <b>Return of the Scarlet Empress</b>, which itself never was referred to save a single (also optional) adventure module and some mechanics on Yozis that the Ebon Dragon introduced. It was more a sort of setting addition that metaplot as many folks use the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, ok. did not know that. <br /> <br /> disregard my comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:07:02-08:00","id":1429969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429848#post1429848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I loved in Trinity Continuum settings, that may be interesting to Exalted, is a \u201cFuture of the Setting\u201d chapter with suggestions to GMs about what may change after year 0 if the characters don\u2019t do anything about. It gives a sense of metaplot without the continual advance of the plot through books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note this is an advent of 2e though. A lot of the things in the timeline of the new corebook were metaplot events. For example, apparently the Jumpers and QMs were just straight-up not in the Aeon 1e corebook I'm told. Jumpers showed up in later sourcebooks, and we never got the QM mechancis. They were going to have rules later, but yeah. This is a good example note of metaplot being weird. In that back in 1e, you had entire splats not exist until later in the line, and the line then would go on talking about them with the rest, incliuding what the currrent organizations think of them, and not what they thought when they were gone. WHich can get annoying for usefulness standpoints.<br /> <br /> To my understanding, the timelines in the books are kind of the broad plans the gameline swere going to go with had they not been closed. Which is good, they're good chapters to have. I just think it's wroth noting that what we have in 2e is a result of hindsight about a much more traditioanlly WW metaplot originally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429848#post1429848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could give hints of how the Civil War would start, or even end, how long it could take, maybe a few ideas for how a reconstruction after the war would go.<br /> <br /> But the main idea is it\u2019s not \u201ccannon\u201d as the ideas are just suggestions to play long runs or even to start campaigns in the aftermath of the war for example. Well, like it was said many times in Trinity forum, Aberrant is the past of Aeon, but Aeon may not be the future of Aberrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an entire chapter on this in the upcoming <b>Heirs to the Shogunate</b>. It's actually pretty neat, including top contenders and due to working more logically, less a &quot;WHo's a big name to smasht ogether like action figures&quot; that I think 2e got trapped in on its Realm civil war hints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:13:24-08:00","id":1429971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KnightFenrirWulfhart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429837#post1429837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> Also, I absolutely love when games have clues and things that are later revealed in metaplot and you're like &quot;I was right?!&quot; Or when a character you hated has had something happen off page and comes back slightly different and you actually get really invested in them. *Chef kiss* ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So in context of RPGs, this point here is actually a big reason a lot of them <i>don't</i> do metaplot, and why Exalted specifcally is trying to avoid it, especially in 3e. Those clues aren't there for fiction writers to fill in and folks to guess what the writers will do. They're there as <i>plot hooks</i>, that shoudl be used by GMs and players to build on for their own campaigns. RPGs aren't really meant to be a mystery novel that you try to outwit the author. They should provide material to allowf or better games. When a plot hook like that is created and then answered later on by the gameline, it in effect &quot;closes off&quot; that plot hook to many tables. While it is intersting to read and youc an ignore it, if it is soemthing that by being open it wasn't talked about, foten when it is closed it gets talked about in ways that make later supplements and books less useful to people in general unless they follow that particular plot line.<br /> <br /> A lot of folks read RPGs for ficiton, and that's fine, but I think folks often forget RPGs should in general probably gear to what's useful for tables. A mantra I remember the current and previous devs had is that if you close off/solve a setting hook, you should introduce soemthing else at least as cool to make up for it. And oftentimes, metaplot is not written in that way, as it treats plot hooks as something later authors can solve, rather than something for tables to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T12:50:26-08:00","id":1429973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429955#post1429955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;741&quot;]I\u2019m a (relative) novice to serious RPG play (as opposed to games in middle school and high school that were more about just hanging out) so I didn\u2019t understand that the power level of the PCs made a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember that &quot;power level&quot; here is directly proportional to the power to change the default state of the setting, rather than how powerful a character is compared to a normal human IRL.<br /> <br /> While there's a correlation between &quot;power&quot; and &quot;power to change the world,&quot; they're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> If you could bring Bruce Wayne into the real world for the purposes of changing the world for the better, but you had to pick Bruce Wayne billionaire CEO, or Batman, but not both? You'd take Bruce Wayne. Bruce's wealth and social influence is far more potent in the real world than Batman's fighting and detective skills will ever be. Bruce's in-universe obsession with being Batman makes him exceedingly more effective at stopping individual instance of bad, but horrible at addressing systemic bad; which has the narrative benefit of meaning Gotham never really changes for long and Batman constantly has enemies new and old to fight.<br /> <br /> A lot of RPGs don't really pay attention to &quot;soft power.&quot; D&amp;D uses gold primarily as a form of XP (though different editions vary this considerably). Early adventures pay out small amounts of gold, limiting your ability to get awesome/magical gear so your stuff stays roughly in line with your Level. As you progress, the challenges get harder, and the payouts bigger, and what stuff you can buy gets more potent. At the same time though, the price of goods, land, and so on doesn't actually change. If the PCs stopped investing in cool gear, and realized their level 18 adventure netted them enough gold to basically buy a kingdom and live comfortable off of taxes, they can start impacting the setting in very drastic ways the default D&amp;D play-styles don't really account for (and the ones that do generally just treat this as the end-state of the campaign).<br /> <br /> Since so many RPGs have PCs gain soft power almost incidentally while focusing on PCs amassing hard power, there's a tendency in RPG talk to treat them as the same (since they will be in a lot of rule sets).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T13:01:11-08:00","id":1429974,"title":"","content":"Wow. I never thought of it that way. Thanks. I guess in Exalted PCs have a lot more soft power than in more traditional RPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T13:11:39-08:00","id":1429975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429974#post1429974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. I never thought of it that way. Thanks. I guess in Exalted PCs have a lot more soft power than in more traditional RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the Exalted do indeed start with a lot more soft power - the Dragon-Blooded, for instance, while mechanically the &quot;weakest&quot; of the Exalted, have pretty huge cultural power built in. Even a Dragon-Blood who doesn't put a single dot into things like Influence, Backing, or any of the rest of social merits, still has the baseline power of <i>being a Dragon-Blood</i>, which many people in the setting will defer to, or have positive feelings towards, by default. And other Dragon-Blooded are more likely to be willing to work with them, compared to any other type of Exalt, and there are many more Dragon-Blooded with actual positions of power and authority in the setting.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Solars probably have the least soft power of any type of Exalt at the start, having no strong cultural traditions of respect and authority to call upon, and a <i>lot</i> of people have active traditions considering them dangerous and untrustworthy. But one of the things that makes Solars (and Abyssals and Infernals) so dangerous to the Dragon-Blooded hegemony is the Solars' skill at very quickly building up their soft power. It rarely takes long for a Solar to make a place for themselves in whatever community, and overcome the traditions working against them through their own force of personality and incredible skills with handling people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T15:23:25-08:00","id":1429987,"title":"","content":"I had blessedly forgotten that THE KUKLAAAAAA!!! had ever existed.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is fine, but it sort of became a meme on the level of \u201cthe sun (as opposed to the Sun God) is a battleship that transforms into a giant mecha\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T16:15:54-08:00","id":1429994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429987#post1429987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had blessedly forgotten that THE KUKLAAAAAA!!! had ever existed.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is fine, but it sort of became a meme on the level of \u201cthe sun (as opposed to the Sun God) is a battleship that transforms into a giant mecha\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really KUKLAAAAAA! unless Chejop Kejak starts crowd surfing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T16:16:41-08:00","id":1429995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429974#post1429974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. I never thought of it that way. Thanks. I guess in Exalted PCs have a lot more soft power than in more traditional RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what Kelly said:<br /> <br /> It's not necessarily that Exalted PCs start with more soft power than most traditional RPGs, but rather than Exalted puts a lot more attention to soft power; both what the PCs can start with, and how they can build it up. You're incentivized to use it, rather than ignore it.<br /> <br /> A great example is that Exalted doesn't just have Merits for interacting with organizations, or have Bureaucracy as a trait, but you can get Bureaucracy magic. Having Exalted run your country is fantastic because they're supernaturally good at making sure all the little aspects of daily life go smoothly. It's also bad because Exalted are flawed human beings with immense power, but that's a slightly different conversation.<br /> <br /> They also have War magic (and war magic, and mind-control magic). But imagine how this impacts things: you can go to war with the Exalted and all their hard power, or play ball with them and benefit from all their soft power. It's far from a perfect world, but like real history, empires like Rome didn't just conquer, they built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T16:24:40-08:00","id":1430000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429995#post1429995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In addition to what Kelly said:<br /> <br /> But imagine how this impacts things: you can go to war with the Exalted and all their hard power, or play ball with them and benefit from all their soft power. It's far from a perfect world, but like real history, empires like Rome didn't just conquer, they built.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your last two sentences make a really good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T19:15:02-08:00","id":1430027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1429971#post1429971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in context of RPGs, this point here is actually a big reason a lot of them <i>don't</i> do metaplot, and why Exalted specifcally is trying to avoid it, especially in 3e. Those clues aren't there for fiction writers to fill in and folks to guess what the writers will do. They're there as <i>plot hooks</i>, that shoudl be used by GMs and players to build on for their own campaigns. RPGs aren't really meant to be a mystery novel that you try to outwit the author. They should provide material to allowf or better games. When a plot hook like that is created and then answered later on by the gameline, it in effect &quot;closes off&quot; that plot hook to many tables. While it is intersting to read and youc an ignore it, if it is soemthing that by being open it wasn't talked about, foten when it is closed it gets talked about in ways that make later supplements and books less useful to people in general unless they follow that particular plot line.<br /> <br /> A lot of folks read RPGs for ficiton, and that's fine, but I think folks often forget RPGs should in general probably gear to what's useful for tables. A mantra I remember the current and previous devs had is that if you close off/solve a setting hook, you should introduce soemthing else at least as cool to make up for it. And oftentimes, metaplot is not written in that way, as it treats plot hooks as something later authors can solve, rather than something for tables to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is certainly true for some, the people I play with have always been able to differentiate between the books and gameplay. It's never been a problem when we play together because we all have to ability to disconnect what we dislike from what we do. Perhaps that's the source of the disagreement. With no metaplot at all you either get a world where you already know everything going on that creates plots, or you have a world where it's almost just game mechanics with a little fluff. <br /> A lot of people like that kind of setting, but I personally find those games don't get well received by the people I play with as it just feels like you only get what you see from the creators. Maybe it's because we're all older school fandom culture members. <br /> Be that what it may, I'd appreciate it if you didn't just assume because I disagree about it must mean I don't play. :]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","user":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","date":"12-26-2020, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T21:01:43-08:00","id":1430044,"title":"","content":"So I'm of two minds about metaplot.<br /> <br /> In practical terms, I think what metaplot does is present multiple, optional versions of the setting. Storytellers always get to choose how to blend them, so it's all more grist for the mill.<br /> <br /> Say there is a metaplot point wherein Gem blows up. If an ST thought Gem was interesting the way it was and wants to use it in a game, it just didn't blow up. If they think the plot elements around it's destruction were cool and wants to use them, Gem hasn't blown up *yet* but probably will when the PCs are around. If the ST likes the aftermath elements, the PCs arrive to find a smoldering crater.<br /> <br /> And these aren't mutally exclusive! That's a big ol' mountain range; if the ST wants to use elements of both plots at the same time, maybe there are two different, culturally related cities-within-volcanos down there (Gem pronouced like &quot;GIF&quot;).<br /> <br /> The downside is that every paragraph describing something that happens to Gem is a paragraph *not* describing somewhere new. And as much as 1e and 2e tried not to have metaplot, they still often gave the impression of a big empty map, because it seemed like a few places (and NPCs...) kept getting name dropped over and over. I might even go so far as to say that 1e and 2e's world building may have suffered because the writers still chose to link books together (and create brand identity...) by reusing elements again and again, *without* the benefit of metaplot to keep them dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 12-27-2020, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T09:56:20-08:00","id":1430241,"title":"","content":"The first setting i played in and ran was legend of the five rings. Besides being the cringiest weeaboo fest on the market, L5R has a mess of a meta plot. Its based on the card game of the same name and the yearly tournaments that happen. Metaplot keeps happening thanks to this card game and the card game tournament events and tbh the meta plot that gets spit out is straight up stupid. I've never run a game set in the present day for it and i always start the game either sometime before the second day of thunder or just after the second day of thunder.<br /> <br /> As far as exalted is concerned, i really appreciate that the setting gives possibilities. I actually didn't like parts of the reclamation plot. Frankly i see the scarlet empresses ambition as far to great to allow her to be the wife and side kick of the ebon dragon, and therefore she'd never settle for less than being empress of all creation herself. Sure many folks talk about the sword of creation requiring some possible sort of human/exalted sacrifice to activate or some infernal power necessary to use it but tbh just never worked for me personally. I prefer it be that mnemon was able to somehow covertly kill her mother out of her own ambition but hasn't been able to consolidate enough power to actually rule the empire.<br /> <br /> I also loved the big open world personally because it made it easy to slap in a number of myriad kingdoms that aren't concerned with what else is going on with the world and run a story that has nothing to do with the rest of the setting other than how they find a way to placate the realm or how they have maintained independence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T11:46:50-08:00","id":1430248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joshopotamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430241#post1430241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first setting i played in and ran was legend of the five rings. Besides being the cringiest weeaboo fest on the market, L5R has a mess of a meta plot. Its based on the card game of the same name and the yearly tournaments that happen. Metaplot keeps happening thanks to this card game and the card game tournament events and tbh the meta plot that gets spit out is straight up stupid. I've never run a game set in the present day for it and i always start the game either sometime before the second day of thunder or just after the second day of thunder.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Had.</i> The current owners reset things for fifth edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T20:12:01-08:00","id":1430298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430248#post1430248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Had.</i> The current owners reset things for fifth edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, one thing one consistently finds in settings with metaplot is later-puublished versions that are resets, because people want the version of the setting from before it was messed up by metaplot.<br /> <br /> The granddaddy of games with metaplot is Traveller. Every version of Traveller's setting published in the last quarter-century is one set in a universe where the published-in-1985 Rebellion and subsequent Virus are irrelevant. Most post-1995 versions use a setting material date prior to the date of the Rebellion, one used an alternate history where the Rebellion never happened, and another uses a centuries-after-the-Rebellion date -- which, in a move of astonishing meta, has your characters spend their time in a VR simulation of the universe from before the Rebellion.<br /> <br /> Fans of settings don't like having the things they liked yanked away by metaplot, whether or not their characters were powerful enough to have any influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T20:26:10-08:00","id":1430302,"title":"","content":"Now you can do adventure modules and stuff without issue. If its decided to do a few small books focusing on the Underworld draining into Creation at an alarming rate that's fine because those books are contained to their own thing and don't have to be referenced by books that are released afterwords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T20:31:53-08:00","id":1430304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430298#post1430298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, one thing one consistently finds in settings with metaplot is later-puublished versions that are resets, because people want the version of the setting from before it was messed up by metaplot.<br /> <br /> The granddaddy of games with metaplot is Traveller. Every version of Traveller's setting published in the last quarter-century is one set in a universe where the published-in-1985 Rebellion and subsequent Virus are irrelevant. Most post-1995 versions use a setting material date prior to the date of the Rebellion, one used an alternate history where the Rebellion never happened, and another uses a centuries-after-the-Rebellion date -- which, in a move of astonishing meta, has your characters spend their time in a VR simulation of the universe from before the Rebellion.<br /> <br /> Fans of settings don't like having the things they liked yanked away by metaplot, whether or not their characters were powerful enough to have any influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your last paragraph makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T08:27:22-08:00","id":1430336,"title":"","content":"I keep on getting partway into typing a response, and then getting distracted or deciding that enough people have answered to the OP's satisfaction.<br /> <br /> And yet here I am.<br /> <br /> Part of it, for me, is that the core has consistently painted an entire world on the brink. On the brink of what? Who knows. But there's a whole delta of rubicons about to get crossed.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of tension there is what I'm saying, and the scale of the game and of its characters means that what happens will run a good chance of affecting your game.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not gonna say metaplot is bad. Orpheus, frex, was nothing but metaplot after the core, with the action of each book moving it forward in major, broadly irreversible ways. But in part that was okay as this was ultimately the story they wanted to tell from the get-go, and it was a contained, limited series.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't have that. It's an open setting for ten thousand stories, and the scale of the action means that an active metaplot ribs a dangerous risk of stumbling into the next Avatar Storm, a plot element in Mage Revised that looked at what had become the default playstyle in second edition and ordered it to stop having fun with such gravelly finality that it murdered Changeling Revised with its banality before it had been written.<br /> <br /> Metaplot isn't good for Exalted. But I do acknowledge that this creates a different weakness, as it closes off a potential avenue for future supplements, and like it or not a game that isn't being actively worked on and produced might not die, but it will fade.<br /> <br /> New editions, then, become the realm of reimagining the setting as it stood at the beginning, refining the mechanics, and also convincing folks that you've done well enough at both that they need to buy the new versions of what they've already got.<br /> <br /> So yeah, even outside of the curiosity regarding the official &quot;what happens next?&quot;, here's plenty of appeal there in the idea of metaplot. But it really doesn't work here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T10:44:47-08:00","id":1430348,"title":"","content":"To summarize what others have been saying: No plot survives contact with the players. Therefore, there has to be room for a metaplot to happen <i>around</i> whatever kinds of adventures the game assumes the players will be having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T13:01:12-08:00","id":1430365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430336#post1430336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep on getting partway into typing a response, and then getting distracted or deciding that enough people have answered to the OP's satisfaction.<br /> <br /> And yet here I am.<br /> <br /> Part of it, for me, is that the core has consistently painted an entire world on the brink. On the brink of what? Who knows. But there's a whole delta of rubicons about to get crossed.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of tension there is what I'm saying, and the scale of the game and of its characters means that what happens will run a good chance of affecting your game.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not gonna say metaplot is bad. Orpheus, frex, was nothing but metaplot after the core, with the action of each book moving it forward in major, broadly irreversible ways. But in part that was okay as this was ultimately the story they wanted to tell from the get-go, and it was a contained, limited series.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't have that. It's an open setting for ten thousand stories, and the scale of the action means that an active metaplot ribs a dangerous risk of stumbling into the next Avatar Storm, a plot element in Mage Revised that looked at what had become the default playstyle in second edition and ordered it to stop having fun with such gravelly finality that it murdered Changeling Revised with its banality before it had been written.<br /> <br /> Metaplot isn't good for Exalted. But I do acknowledge that this creates a different weakness, as it closes off a potential avenue for future supplements, and like it or not a game that isn't being actively worked on and produced might not die, but it will fade.<br /> <br /> New editions, then, become the realm of reimagining the setting as it stood at the beginning, refining the mechanics, and also convincing folks that you've done well enough at both that they need to buy the new versions of what they've already got.<br /> <br /> So yeah, even outside of the curiosity regarding the official &amp;quot;what happens next?&amp;quot;, here's plenty of appeal there in the idea of metaplot. But it really doesn't work here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you anyway \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T13:43:02-08:00","id":1430367,"title":"","content":"I was talking about N/A artifacts and I remembered this gem from the 1E Storyteller's Companion:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://bayimg.com/2c10a0ec1a2bfcf652b1100414fb8c886198bede.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-30-2020, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T17:25:40-08:00","id":1430394,"title":"","content":"Why\u2019d you repeat the same image three times? EDIT: Fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 12-30-2020, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T20:43:37-08:00","id":1430410,"title":"","content":"Fundamentally, an RPG book is not a novel. It should not be treated as one. To do so without compromising its capability as an RPG book is difficult to say the least. <br /> At the core of it, every word you (the author) spend telling me what other characters are doing is a word you aren't telling the player what they could be doing. In fact, it's not even neutral, it's negative. My character can't do that because this other character already did. <br /> While I acknowledge the point made upthread by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25226\" data-vbnamecard=\"25226\">KnightFenrirWulfhart</a> that a metaplot development isn't that different from a splatbook or setting book when it comes to invalidating existing campaigns, there is difference in how predictable it is. I can know that, for example, setting a game in Jiara is going to require me to have to make up a lot about Jiara, as no setting book that covers it in more than just a few paragraphs has yet been released. This is something I know, something I can plan around. It's something entirely different when I pick up the latest book to discover that Jiara was wiped off the map in the latest update. More broadly, setting and splat books tend to expand on what's already there, while metaplot tends to change what's already there.<br /> Finally, every defender of metaplot ever has defended it with &quot;well if you don't like it, just don't use it!&quot; The problem with that is that it's in the book, taking up wordcount. It's expected that it will be used, because if it wasn't, then why would the authors and developers put it in? How much extra am I paying for 5k words that expand on a metaplot I'm not using? What else could those 5k words have been used for? How much utility is this book, this book that is ostensibly meant to help me play a game, sacrificing to tell me stories about characters that I don't play doing things that I can't do. <br /> If you want a gripping fictional narrative in your game world, then read fiction. Read a tie-in novel, or a fanfic. Don't make my game books worse by making them pull double duty as novels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T23:35:26-08:00","id":1430421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430410#post1430410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the core of it, every word you (the author) spend telling me what other characters are doing is a word you aren't telling the player what they could be doing. In fact, it's not even neutral, it's negative. My character can't do that because this other character already did.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this can be true for very broad things like a metaplot, for fiction pieces in the books (even ones that have a minor ongoing story such as different adventures of the signature characters) the authors are using word count to communicate to players what their characters can do in the game. Fiction pieces help communicate the intentions of the developers by showing it via narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, every defender of metaplot ever has defended it with &quot;well if you don't like it, just don't use it!&quot; The problem with that is that it's in the book, taking up wordcount. </div> </div> </div>To an extent, though I offered a defense of metaplot that directly addresses this concern: metaplot only happens in metaplot books that you'd only be buying because you enjoy following the metaplot; thus the optional nature of it is actualized effectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't make my game books worse by making them pull double duty as novels. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's asking gaming books to be novels. However putting fiction pieces in gaming books is clearly of value to enough customers that gaming companies keep doing it. The issues with metaplot are when things start stringing together between books, not when there's fiction in one book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-30T18:48:48-08:00","id":1430521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430421#post1430421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this can be true for very broad things like a metaplot, for fiction pieces in the books (even ones that have a minor ongoing story such as different adventures of the signature characters) the authors are using word count to communicate to players what their characters can do in the game. Fiction pieces help communicate the intentions of the developers by showing it via narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To an extent, though I offered a defense of metaplot that directly addresses this concern: metaplot only happens in metaplot books that you'd only be buying because you enjoy following the metaplot; thus the optional nature of it is actualized effectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nobody's asking gaming books to be novels. However putting fiction pieces in gaming books is clearly of value to enough customers that gaming companies keep doing it. The issues with metaplot are when things start stringing together between books, not when there's fiction in one book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is true, For an example, the brief fiction piece about the Vendetta in the House Iselsi section of WFHW. Written as a fiction piece because the author couldn't get it to work as anything else. <br /> <br /> I think Cthulhutech did it that way, with all the metaplot in a few dedicated metaplot books. Definitely the way I'd do it, if I had to. <br /> <br /> More specifically, I'd say the big problem is when the interconnected fiction is in the present, and (especially) covering major events. Reading about Tepet Arada killing Fear Eater? Big, but in the past. Strawmaiden Janest facing off against a Raksha horde? Big for her, not for Creation. My rule of thumb is that game fiction should inspire &quot;I wanna do that!&quot;, not &quot;Why couldn't I have been the one to do that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T06:27:38-08:00","id":1430661,"title":"","content":"Metaplots probably aren't like, objectively bad<br /> <br /> But I have yet to see what in a gameline that I thought added to the gameline, rather than detracting from it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T13:38:03-08:00","id":1430911,"title":"","content":"Metaplots are already a bit shaky for something on the power scale of, say, D&amp;D, but when you try to apply one to Exalted, a game where the expected PC is capable of single-handedly changing the <i>entire setting</i> with enough effort, it really doesn't work. A Solar Circle can straight up topple empires, uncover grand lost secrets, form their own empire, and go as far as <i>fundamentally changing the foundation of existence</i>. This is also why pre-made adventures don't work for Exalted--or at least, for Solars--because PC's can often just utterly smash through what would be narratively interesting roadblocks in other systems with their supernal skill (now, an adventure for DB's...that might be able to work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T14:25:20-08:00","id":1430916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429791-why-doesn\u2019t-exalted-have-a-metaplot?p=1430367#post1430367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about N/A artifacts and I remembered this gem from the 1E Storyteller's Companion:</div> </div> </div> </div>That middle quote, specifically, has stuck with me through the years and across editions. Thanks for digging that up; I couldn't remember if it was from that book or one of the developer q&amp;a's or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T15:42:12-08:00","id":1430928,"title":"","content":"Looking at that line from the Storyteller's Companion, I find myself considering that I don't own enough First Edition books to know if it's something that they ever quite followed through on.<br /> <br /> I have seen plenty of quotes from freelancers archived from forums in which they make statements that make more sense as allusions to events planned to be in future books (revelations of the Scarlet Empress as the Bride of the Ebon Dragon figure prominently among them), but I'm still curious how much was ever implemented or if it was a plan that ended up being phased out a bit.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress stuff at least gets a throughline across Exalted: The Dragon-Blooded, Games of Divinity and Aspect Book: Earth...<br /> <br /> In any case, reading that statement does make me think of how I've a fondness for when the inter-chapter fictions continuously develop storylines. Even in Second Edition comics, a format I'm otherwise critical of; I have a particular fondness for the serial nature of most stuff there involving Arianna, borne from a period where I was compelled to go back and examine as much stuff as I had possession of to interrogate the popular narrative of her as a reprehensible character.<br /> <br /> Although I think about that and find myself thinking that even if Exalted did commit itself to a World of Darkness-style metaplot, some of the setting composition would need to be reformatted to make it work. I feel as though part of what drives metaplot in something like Vampire: the Masquerade is that there are these massive institutions encompassing the world, some of which are even centrally controlled* to provide an arena in which trends can play out or the ambitions of major individuals can radiate, where Exalted has far less of that even at points where the world seems smallest, and certainly not so much right now. The Exalted and even the Scarlet Realm may be very powerful, but it's ultimately not a world deeply interconnected by globalization, and I think that makes the impact of certain dramatic events slower to roll out. You could publish future supplements in which the Realm Civil War is actually underway, but I feel as though writers might struggle with the matter that plausibly there would be large sections of the world in which that isn't really felt.<br /> <br /> Which might be why the most metaplot like thing they ever pulled off actually was &quot;the Yozis manipulating world events to create conditions for their return, including an outcome where one of them actually pulls it off&quot;. I do think there's something telling in how the writers who actually put that together ended up looking back on it with reservations and disliking the implications of writing in characters who could create a metaplot big enough for the whole world.<br /> <br /> Heh, kind of followed the Golden Path to create a world that would be more proof against metaplot; break down the God-Emperors and scatter the populace across a much wider expanse.<br /> <br /> * At least up until the metaplot develops into a big world and game building element of &quot;the central control has broken down and your local chapter has more autonomy than any in living memory&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T16:46:38-08:00","id":1430932,"title":"","content":"Something worth remembering too is that in WoD even, there wasn't a big book of secrets somewhere where they had this grand plan. I remember this when <b>Gehenna </b>came out in 2003. As it turns out, authors just kind of kept making shit up as it went along and by the tiemt hey had to wrap things up, stuff could get weird as they tried to do so.<br /> <br /> To some extent, this is probably the gist of the entire thing with the Empress in 1e. Note it didn't like, <i>go anywhere</i> in 1e, becuase the gameline wasn't itnerested in it at th eend of the day save as a neat potential story thread. And the authors of the events in 2e were not the same ones writing for 1e most of the time, and so it was basically interpreation of previous stuff going places it felt like. It's not some great settings ecret being revealed but just kind of a general wirter's Round Robin. Which while interesting in ficiton, agian, isn't something wordcount in books I think is best spent on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}